{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794313851,"nonce":"wpYfJO23alknvrcYCkm/524duBE=","title":"Idle windows keep committing frames: Calendar commits 60 surfaces per second with no input, Tasks about 22","message":"Measured in the live probe (nested kwin_wayland --virtual, 60 Hz virtual output, no input after start, WAYLAND_DEBUG=client counting wl_surface.commit over 10 s after 8 s of settling, /proc/\u003cpid\u003e/stat for CPU; debug builds, one machine):\n- fs-calendar (Blinc at PR 71 head, month view, nothing hovered): 600 commits in 10 s (60 per second), 1.41 s CPU in 10 s.\n- fs-tasks (blinc-app-fix fork, list view, no focus): 224 commits in 10 s, 1.07 s CPU in 10 s.\nA window with no input and no running animation should commit nothing (ControlFlow::Wait). The cause is not yet found; candidates to check, not established: a CSS animation or spring that never settles, a canvas draw callback re-run every frame (see issue ea7d722), or a redraw request that re-arms itself.\n\nGoal (owner): only what changes is computed and drawn, idle produces no frame, 120 fps (8.3 ms) when something does change.\nReproducer: /srv/FreeSynergy/.scratch/b-probe/idle.sh \u003capp\u003e inside run.sh of the live probe (fs-components tools/live-probe).\nProposal for the maintainer, no PR before agreement: find what keeps requesting frames while idle, and make the frame loop stop when nothing is dirty.","files":null}]}